WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.667
This burned scroll was

2
00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:03.300
too fragile to open.

3
00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:04.967
Scientists read it anyway.

4
00:00:05.367 --> 00:00:06.900
The En-Gedi scroll crumbled

5
00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:08.400
when it was touched.

6
00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:11.100
Researchers scanned it
with X-rays,

7
00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:13.100
building a
three-dimensional map.

8
00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:14.667
Inside that scan,

9
00:00:14.667 --> 00:00:16.967
they traced
the surviving layers.

10
00:00:17.167 --> 00:00:18.200
In this scroll,

11
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:20.300
the ink showed up
more densely

12
00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:21.333
than the parchment.

13
00:00:21.533 --> 00:00:23.300
They mapped that signal

14
00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:24.633
onto digital surfaces,

15
00:00:24.633 --> 00:00:25.967
then flattened them

16
00:00:25.967 --> 00:00:27.300
into readable images.

17
00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:29.233
The recovered Hebrew text

18
00:00:29.233 --> 00:00:31.567
came from the
Book of Leviticus.

19
00:00:31.767 --> 00:00:33.100
This worked because

20
00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:36.200
the ink was detectable
in the scan.

21
00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:38.400
Different materials need
different approaches.

22
00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:40.800
They revealed
surviving writing

23
00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:43.567
without unrolling
the fragile original.
